# Render Deployment - Environment Variables

## Required Variables (Set these in Render Dashboard)

# Database Configuration
# Render will automatically provide MONGODB_URI from the connected MongoDB database
MONGODB_URI=your-mongodb-connection-string

# Server Configuration
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=5001

# Authentication
JWT_SECRET=your-super-secret-jwt-key-generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
JWT_EXPIRE=7d

# CORS Configuration
CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-frontend-domain.com

# Admin Credentials (for initial setup)
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@hydrogrid.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-this-secure-password

# Email Configuration (Optional)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-app-password

# API Configuration
API_TIMEOUT=30000
MAX_REQUEST_SIZE=10mb

# Monitoring (Optional)
LOG_LEVEL=info
SENTRY_DSN=your-sentry-dsn-for-error-tracking

---

## How to Setup on Render

1. Connect your GitHub repository to Render
2. Create a new Web Service with:
   - **Name**: HydroGrid
   - **Environment**: Node
   - **Region**: Oregon (US West)
   - **Branch**: main
   - **Root Directory**: server
   - **Build Command**: npm install
   - **Start Command**: npm start
   - **Instance**: Free tier (512MB RAM, 0.1 CPU)

3. Under "Environment" tab, add these variables:
   ```
   NODE_ENV: production
   PORT: 5001
   JWT_SECRET: (generate with: openssl rand -base64 32)
   ADMIN_EMAIL: admin@hydrogrid.com
   ADMIN_PASSWORD: your-secure-password
   ```

4. Add MongoDB database:
   - Click "Create Database"
   - Name: hydrogrid-db
   - Plan: Free
   - Region: Oregon
   - Database Name: hydrogrid
   - Render will auto-inject MONGODB_URI

5. Deploy and monitor from Render dashboard

---

## Generate Secure JWT Secret

```bash
# On your machine, run:
openssl rand -base64 32

# Output example:
# aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ1234567890+/==

# Copy this to Render's JWT_SECRET environment variable
```

---

## Post-Deployment Setup

1. **Run Database Seed Script**:
   - SSH into Render service
   - Run: `npm run seed`
   - This will populate test data

2. **Test API**:
   ```bash
   curl https://hydrogrid.onrender.com/api/health
   ```

3. **Login with Test Credentials**:
   - Email: admin@hydrogrid.com
   - Password: (set in ADMIN_PASSWORD)

4. **Monitor Logs**:
   - View real-time logs in Render dashboard

---

## Pricing & Limits

| Tier | Cost | RAM | CPU | Disk | Best For |
|------|------|-----|-----|------|----------|
| Free | $0 | 512 MB | 0.1 | 1 GB | Development |
| Starter | $7 | 512 MB | 0.5 | 1 GB | Small apps |
| Standard | $25 | 2 GB | 1 | 10 GB | Production |
| Pro | $85 | 4 GB | 2 | 20 GB | High traffic |

**Free tier limitations**:
- Spins down after 15 min inactivity
- Auto-restarts (cold start ~1 min)
- Good for demos/testing

**Upgrade when needed** for:
- Always-on availability
- Better performance
- Persistent storage
- SSH access

---

## Troubleshooting

### Service won't start
- Check logs in Render dashboard
- Verify MongoDB connection string
- Ensure all environment variables are set

### Cold starts are too long
- Upgrade to Starter tier (persistent container)
- Optimize Node.js startup time

### Database connection fails
- Verify MONGODB_URI format
- Check MongoDB database is accessible
- Confirm database credentials

### CORS errors
- Set CORS_ORIGIN to your frontend domain
- Add to environment variables

---

## Health Check

Render will automatically health check at:
```
GET https://hydrogrid.onrender.com/api/health
```

Ensure your server responds with 200 status.

---

## Auto-Deploy Setup

Render automatically deploys when:
- You push to 'main' branch
- GitHub Actions complete successfully
- No breaking changes in dependencies

To disable auto-deploy:
- Go to Service Settings → Deploy
- Uncheck "Auto-Deploy"

---

**Next Steps**: Visit https://dashboard.render.com to create your service!
